3049-10     Summary
3050-Set f, g : C2 → C polynomials. We say that (f, g) is a Jacobian pair if its
3051-Jacobian determinant is a non-zero constant. The plane Jacobian conjecture
3052-asserts that any Jacobian pair is an automorphism of C2 .
3053-   For any polynomials f, g : C2 → C one can find d ∈ N, such that
3054-#(f, g)−1 (z) = d for generic z ∈ C2 . This number td(f, g) := d is called
3055:the topological degree of (f, g).
3056:   Orevkov and Domrina proved that if (f, g) is a counterexample of the
3057-Jacobian conjecture, then td(f, g) 6= 3 and td(f, g) 6= 4 cf. [O2], [D] and
3058-[D-O].
3059-The main result of this thesis is:
3060:Theorem 9.1 Assume that (f, g) is a counterexample of the plane Jacobian
3061-conjecture. Then td(f, g) ≥ 6.
